(The Purchasing System - A Teaching Guide for Office Mates) Tj T*
(Who this is for: office staff who are not computer people. No jargon, no tech talk - just what to click and what it means.) Tj T*
(What the system does, in one sentence: it keeps track of everything from "we need to buy medicines" all the way to "the items arrived and are counted" - in one place, so nothing is forgotten and every peso is accounted for.) Tj T*
(---) Tj T*
(Part 1 - The Big Picture \(tell them this first\)) Tj T*
(Every purchase in the office follows the same road. Think of it like ordering food: you decide what you want, you ask for the price, you compare, you order, and then the food arrives. Our system does the same steps, just with medicines and supplies.) Tj T*
(The 6 stops on the road:) Tj T*
(```) Tj T*
(1. PROJECTS   ->  "What do we need to buy, and for which office?") Tj T*
(2. PREPLIST   ->  "Put everything we need on one shopping list.") Tj T*
(3. QUOTATION  ->  "Ask suppliers: how much? Then collect their answers.") Tj T*
(4. Item Catalog->  "Compare the answers. Who is cheapest? Who has the freshest stock?") Tj T*
(5. PURCHASE   ->  "Give the winning supplier the official order.") Tj T*
(ORDER) Tj T*
(6. RECEIVING  ->  "Items arrive. Check them off. Done.") Tj T*
(```) Tj T*
(That's it. Everything else - searching, printing, deleting, settings - is just detail on top of these six stops.) Tj T*
(---) Tj T*
(Part 2 - Signing In and Signing Out) Tj T*
(1. Open the browser and go to the office computer address given by your administrator.) Tj T*
(2. Type your username and password, then click Log in.) Tj T*
(3. You will see a page with a dark-green panel on the left side. That panel is your menu.) Tj T*
(4. To leave: click your profile photo / name at the top of the side panel, then Sign out.) Tj T*
(Good habits to teach:) Tj T*
(o Never share your password with anyone, even the administrator.) Tj T*
(o If you are away from your desk, sign out. The system signs you out automatically if you sit idle too long - that's a safety feature, not a bug.) Tj T*
(o If you forgot your password, ask the administrator to make a new one for you. Do not ask your officemates to let you use theirs.) Tj T*
(---) Tj T*
(Part 3 - Your Role in the System) Tj T*
(Not everyone can do everything. This is on purpose - think of it as keys to a filing cabinet.) Tj T*
(| What you can do | What it means |) Tj T*
(|---|---|) Tj T*
(| View | You can look at everything, but change nothing. Buttons look grey and "can't be clicked." |) Tj T*
(| Manage | You can add, edit, upload, send, receive - the full work. |) Tj T*
(| Administrator | Everything, plus the Settings page \(accounts, passwords, privileges\). |) Tj T*
(Teaching tip: if a colleague says "the button is grey and won't click," the answer is always: *"You have View access. Ask the administrator if you need to change things."* No other explanation is needed.) Tj T*
(---) Tj T*
(Part 4 - A Walkthrough of Each Module \(left panel, top to bottom\)) Tj T*
(4.1 PROJECTS - "The job we are going to do") Tj T*
(What this is in real life: when the office awards a contract \(shopping, small value, competitive bidding, direct contracting\), the details go here. Example: *"Purchase of Medicines for Dao"* - DOH Region 6, December 2026.) Tj T*
(What's on the screen:) Tj T*
(o The project title, its reference number, how much was awarded, the date, how many days the supplier has to deliver, and whether delivery is overdue.) Tj T*
(o A list of items needed \(e.g., Mefenamic 500mg, 256 boxes\) and how many remain to be procured.) Tj T*
(o Buttons to Add project, Edit, Delete, and Print Project \(which prints a printout in 8.5 × 13 in officio, landscape - the standard government size\).) Tj T*
(What to say to your colleagues:) Tj T*
(> "A project is the whole job - who bought, what for, how much, and what's in it. If something is in a project, it means it is real and budgeted.") Tj T*
(4.2 PREPLIST - "The shopping list we are actually buying from") Tj T*
(What this is in real life: Projects show *everything* planned. Not all of it gets bought at once. The Preplist is the list of what we will buy this time.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
