stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL
50 780 Td
(What you can do here:) Tj T*
(o Compile a prep list - pick the items from one or more projects, and the system merges them into one list with a number like PL-2026-0001.) Tj T*
(o For each item, you can set the minimum shelf life \(in months\) remaining at delivery - important for medicines. `0 = non-perishable`.) Tj T*
(o The list is collapsible - click a project to expand its items; click again to collapse.) Tj T*
(o You can type Notes \(e.g., "deliver before Christmas"\) - optional.) Tj T*
(What to say to your colleagues:) Tj T*
(> "Think of Projects as your fridge plan for the whole month. The Preplist is what goes into this week's grocery cart.") Tj T*
(4.3 QUOTATION - "Ask, receive, and compare") Tj T*
(This is the busiest screen. Three stages happen here:) Tj T*
(Stage A - Send the Request for Quotation \(RFQ\)) Tj T*
(1. Open the prep list.) Tj T*
(2. Click Generate RFQ.) Tj T*
(3. Tick the suppliers you want to invite.) Tj T*
(4. The system creates a file for each supplier and downloads it. That file is a form with the item names, units, and required shelf life - but no quantities. \(Suppliers must not know how much we need, that's our rule.\)) Tj T*
(5. Print or email the file to the suppliers.) Tj T*
(Stage B - Supplier sends us back their answer) Tj T*
(o When a supplier returns their form, upload it here. The system reads the quoted prices and stores them - their answer is now part of the system.) Tj T*
(o You will see for each supplier: their answer, their status \(e.g., "responded"\), and whether it can be compared yet.) Tj T*
(Stage C - Compare and award) Tj T*
(o Look at Item Catalog \(next section\) to decide who wins per item.) Tj T*
(o Once awarded, click Proceed to PO - that starts the Purchase Order.) Tj T*
(Buttons you will see on the Quotation page:) Tj T*
(o Submit quotation / Replace - upload or swap the supplier's file.) Tj T*
(o Download - get the supplier's file back.) Tj T*
(o Remove - delete the uploaded file only \(not the whole quotation\).) Tj T*
(o Delete - remove this supplier's quotation entirely. Blocked if linked to a purchase order - ask the administrator.) Tj T*
(o Proceed to PO - start the purchase order with the awarded suppliers.) Tj T*
(What to say to your colleagues:) Tj T*
(> "Stage A is us asking. Stage B is them answering. Stage C is us saying yes. If you are at Stage B without a file uploaded, do not proceed anywhere else.") Tj T*
(4.4 Item Catalog - "Who is the best deal?") Tj T*
(What this is in real life: the comparison table.) Tj T*
(For every item on the prep list, you see:) Tj T*
(o Best price - the cheapest price that a supplier quoted.) Tj T*
(o Best expiry - the supplier offering the freshest stock.) Tj T*
(o Best price board - a ranking of suppliers by how many items they won.) Tj T*
(o The premium column shows how many percent each supplier is more expensive than the best price. Example: `+5.0% vs best` means they're 5% more expensive than the cheapest.) Tj T*
(o Lowest price is highlighted in green.) Tj T*
(Suggestion, not decision. The system suggests the lowest price; it never picks for you. If you want a different supplier for an item - closer relationship, fresher stock, better delivery - open the item on the board and click Add to cart on that supplier's row. Your pick wins. Swapping to another supplier replaces the line in the cart before checkout. "Add best prices to cart" \(and the per-row cart buttons\) are one-click suggestions for the common case of wanting the lowest price.) Tj T*
(Teaching tip: do not let anyone stare at one supplier and pick by feeling. The board exists so the decision is visible and defendable: *"We picked them because they won 8 out of 10 items at the best price."*) Tj T*
(What to say to your colleagues:) Tj T*
(> "Item Catalog is not a ranking of who's friendly. It's the scoreboard. Because we all have to answer to our auditor: which suppliers won, and why.") Tj T*
(4.5 PURCHASE ORDER - "The official yes") Tj T*
(What this is in real life: the document the office gives the winning supplier saying: *"We will buy from you. Here is what, how much, when."*) Tj T*
(What you can do here:) Tj T*
(o See the PO number, the supplier, the items and the agreed prices.) Tj T*
(o Send the PO to the supplier.) Tj T*
(o Cancel the PO if the deal falls through \(only before items are received\).) Tj T*
(o When items arrive, mark them as received, one by one. Quantity, unit, price - everything is locked once you confirm receipt.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
