(o The PO keeps track of partial deliveries too \(e.g., 128 of 250 boxes delivered today\).) Tj T*
(What to say to your colleagues:) Tj T*
(> "The PO is our promise in writing. The minute the supplier sees it, they can buy the stock. After that, changing anything is a lot of paperwork - so double-check before clicking Send.") Tj T*
(4.6 ENTITIES - "The other offices and the suppliers") Tj T*
(Two kinds of contacts live here:) Tj T*
(o Procuring entities - the government offices that buy \(e.g., DOH Region 6, hospital supply divisions\).) Tj T*
(o Suppliers - the companies that sell to us \(e.g., ABC Pharma, XYZ Medicals\).) Tj T*
(Each profile shows their name, type, address, contact person, and transaction history. You can Add, Edit, or Delete - but not delete one that has been used in a real PO \(the system protects the record trail\).) Tj T*
(What to say to your colleagues:) Tj T*
(> "This is our address book. If an office or supplier changes address or contact number, update it here once - everyone sees the new one.") Tj T*
(4.7 SETTINGS - "The administrator's cabinet" \(administrators only\)) Tj T*
(If you are not the administrator, you will never see this. If you are, this is where you:) Tj T*
(o Users & Privileges - create accounts, reset passwords, turn accounts on/off.) Tj T*
(o Module access - decide who can View and who can Manage, per module.) Tj T*
(o Activity logs - every action anyone did in the system, with who and when \("deleted Project RF-2026-0042", "edited Preplist PL-2026-0001"\).) Tj T*
(o Backup - download a copy of everything, just in case.) Tj T*
(What to say to your colleagues:) Tj T*
(> "Settings is the principal's office. If something needs changing there, bring it to me - don't start poking around on your own.") Tj T*
(---) Tj T*
(Part 5 - A 45-Minute Teaching Script \(use this in the actual training\)) Tj T*
(Run this exactly as written the first time. Keep it hands-on - every learner should hold the mouse at least once.) Tj T*
(0:00-0:05 - Why we have this) Tj T*
(> "We're going to walk through one real purchase: medicines for Dao. In 40 minutes you'll see every step the system handles, from the order to the delivery receipt.") Tj T*
(0:05-0:10 - Sign in and look around) Tj T*
(> "Type your username and password. See the dark panel on the left? That's our menu. Count the buttons: Projects, Preplist, Quotation, Item Catalog, Purchase Order, Entities, Settings. Everything lives in one of those seven.") Tj T*
(0:10-0:18 - Projects \(the big picture\)) Tj T*
(1. Click Projects.) Tj T*
(2. Point out: title, reference number, amount awarded, deliver-by date, list of items and how many remain.) Tj T*
(3. Click one project to open it. Show the Print Project button and print a copy - hand it to a learner.) Tj T*
(4. Say: *"This printout is what we attach to our filing. It has the 8.5 × 13 in officio format - same size as our other government forms."*) Tj T*
(0:18-0:26 - Preplist \(the shopping list\)) Tj T*
(1. Click Preplist -> Compile prep list.) Tj T*
(2. Tick one project and tick its items.) Tj T*
(3. Set a shelf life for one medicine \(e.g., 12 months\). Set 0 for a non-perishable \(equipment\).) Tj T*
(4. Click Compile. Show the new number \(e.g., `PL-2026-0001`\).) Tj T*
(5. Say: *"Notice: no quantities will be printed for the suppliers. They see the item and the unit and the shelf life - that's all. We never show how much we're buying."*) Tj T*
(0:26-0:34 - Quotation \(the ask and the answer\)) Tj T*
(1. Open the prep list -> Generate RFQ.) Tj T*
(2. Tick 2 suppliers -> Download. Open the file. Show that there are no quantities - only items, units, and required shelf life.) Tj T*
(3. Say: *"This file goes to the suppliers. When they answer, we upload it here - that's Stage B."*) Tj T*
(4. Upload a dummy supplier file \(prepare two before the session: save the RFQ downloads from step 2, then fill each copy in with made-up prices, brands, and expiry dates - that is exactly the file a supplier would return; sample RFQ/PO printouts no longer ship with the repository\).) Tj T*
(5. Show Submit quotation and Replace.) Tj T*
(0:34-0:40 - Item Catalog \(the decision\)) Tj T*
(1. Click Item Catalog.) Tj T*
(2. Walk through the Best price board and the columns: Best price, Best expiry, premium vs best.) Tj T*
(3. Say: *"Green cells are the cheapest. These percentages are how much more expensive the other offers are. If the cheapest file has no prices yet - they haven't answered."*) Tj T*
(0:40-0:44 - Purchase Order \(the official yes\)) Tj T*
(1. Back to the awarded quotation -> Proceed to PO.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
