(2. Check the items \(only awarded ones come across\) and Send the PO.) Tj T*
(3. Show the Receive button on the items - demo ticking one received.) Tj T*
(4. Say: *"Click this only when the boxes are physically in your hands and counted. Once ticked, it cannot be unticked casually."*) Tj T*
(0:44-0:45 - Questions) Tj T*
(Take the questions. If a question needs 5+ minutes to answer, write it down and say you'll answer in the next session - do not improvise.) Tj T*
(---) Tj T*
(Part 6 - Rules to Teach From Day One) Tj T*
(1. Nothing is deleted lightly. Anti-delete warnings exist for a reason - a PO that anything is linked to cannot be deleted. Ask the administrator if you hit that wall.) Tj T*
(2. Quantities are never given to suppliers. Only item, unit, shelf life.) Tj T*
(3. Shelf life is in months, always, and `0 = non-perishable`.) Tj T*
(4. If something looks wrong, stop. Do not "fix" it by deleting and redoing. Ask the administrator or the system officer.) Tj T*
(5. Gray buttons are intentional. You don't have permission to do that - ask, don't force.) Tj T*
(6. Printouts go in the official folder. The printout is the official copy, not a screen grab.) Tj T*
(---) Tj T*
(Part 7 - Quick Answers to Questions You Will Hear) Tj T*
("Why can't I see the quantity on the supplier's form?") Tj T*
(Because suppliers should never know how many we need. That protects our bidding.) Tj T*
("This supplier answered by hand - can I type it in?") Tj T*
(No. The system reads the file itself, so nobody can accidentally key in the wrong number. Ask the supplier to fill the computer file. If absolutely impossible, the administrator can help.) Tj T*
("Can I undo a receipt?") Tj T*
(No. Receipt is final. If you made a mistake, tell the administrator - that's what their override exists for.) Tj T*
("Where's the data if the computer dies?") Tj T*
(The administrator makes regular backups from Settings -> Backup. Your work is not kept only on your PC.) Tj T*
("Can two of us work at the same time?") Tj T*
(Yes. That's the point of the system - one office, one set of records.) Tj T*
("Who do I call when the screen looks weird?") Tj T*
(Your system administrator. Take a screenshot with your phone if possible - it helps.) Tj T*
(---) Tj T*
(Part 8 - Glossary in Plain Words) Tj T*
(| Word | What it means here |) Tj T*
(|---|---|) Tj T*
(| Project | One whole purchase job - contract, budget, items. |) Tj T*
(| Preplist | The shopping list we buy *this* time. |) Tj T*
(| RFQ | The request we send suppliers: "how much per item?" |) Tj T*
(| Quotation | The supplier's answer to that request. |) Tj T*
(| Item Catalog | The comparison table of all the answers. |) Tj T*
(| Best price | The cheapest unit price a supplier offered. |) Tj T*
(| Best expiry | The supplier offering the freshest stock. |) Tj T*
(| Purchase Order \(PO\) | The official order given to the winning supplier. |) Tj T*
(| Receive | Ticking that the boxes physically arrived. |) Tj T*
(| Fulfillment | How much of a project is done, in percent. |) Tj T*
(| View | You can look, not touch. |) Tj T*
(| Manage | You can work on it. |) Tj T*
(| Reference no. | The number the system gave it \(e.g., `PL-2026-0001`, `RFQ-2026-0042`\). Write it on every printout. |) Tj T*
(---) Tj T*
(Part 9 - One-Minute Summary \(for the closing of the session\)) Tj T*
(> "Look at the purchase like a single story. A project in Projects is a job we were given. The Preplist is the list we chose to buy. The Quotation is how we asked the suppliers and what they answered. The Item Catalog is how we decided. The Purchase Order is the yes we gave. Receiving is when the goods arrived. Every screen in this system is just one chapter of that one story - if you remember the story, you can find everything.") Tj T*
ET
